>   With all the constant talk of stemming NH abuse I'm surprised no one
>has ever complained about the ability of an athame to engrave Elbereth
>indefinitely. I recently began to play wizards and I was quite impressed
>by the power of this feature. Properly executed I found it a lot more
>destabilizing than polypiling or a ring of conflict, especially in the
>early game where survival is most difficult. Any comments?

Yes, just one: give it a rest.  It drives me crazy to see constant
cries of "ABUSE!!  ABUSE!!  ABUSE!!  BURN IT ALIVE, DEV TEAM!  HANG
IT!  ABUSE!!" in this newsgroup.  It seems that some people are
hellbent on taking all the fun out of Nethack.  Yes, engraving the
evil E-word with an athame is very helpful, but it doesn't last
forever if you fight, and Wizards start out so wimpy that it's *very*
difficult for them to survive the beginning of the game without this
protection.  Before I was aware of this feature, I was only able to
get one or two wizards past the first five or six levels, and this was
during my period of intense Nethack addiction (which, thank god, is
over--again!  :) ).

So this is just one person's plea:  *please* let's not turn this into
another abuse debate.  Or, if this does turn into a big abuse debate,
please, dev team, close your eyes and plug your ears!!

